{#
  ★★ THE STANDING RULE FOR EVERY BLOCK IN THIS FOLDER (user, 2026-09-08):
  ENFORCE, DO NOT NEGATE.

      wrong: "you cannot remove this device if you don't have the key"
      right: "this device can only be removed with the proper key and will
              stay on otherwise"

  The user's reasoning, and it matches what 0792 recorded back in August ("LLM
  do really bad with negative, make them focus on what not to do and end up
  doing it"): a prohibition still puts the forbidden thing in the model's
  context, described in detail, and a model that has just read a vivid
  description of clean dialogue is more likely to write clean dialogue.

  HOW THIS WAS APPLIED, so the pattern is reusable:
    * "Do NOT write intelligible dialogue"  -> "EVERY line she gives is pure
      vocalisation" - say what the output IS, not what it must avoid.
    * "Do NOT have her recognise a person by sight" -> "everything she knows
      about the room arrives through hearing, touch, smell and memory" - give
      the channel that IS open and the closed one needs no mention.
    * "she cannot use her hands" -> "her hands are held out of use" - the same
      fact as a state of the body rather than a missing ability.
    * "It does not come off on its own" -> "It stays exactly as it was put on
      ... time is on the device's side."

  ⚠ AUDITED TO ZERO on 2026-09-08: no "do not / never / cannot / can not /
  no longer" survives in the RENDERED prose of any of the nine blocks. Comments
  like this one are exempt - they are read by people, not by the model.
  Re-run the check before shipping a prompt edit; it is trivial to regress.

  ★ ONE DELIBERATE SURVIVOR, and it is a different kind of word: this file's
  ring-gag header still reads "SPEECH IS BADLY DEGRADED, NOT BLOCKED". That is
  a CONTRAST that tells the model which of two mutually exclusive states it is
  in, not a prohibition on behaviour. Removing it would let a ring gag be
  played as a sealed one. The rule is about instructions, not about every
  occurrence of the word.
#}
{#
  ★★ RENUMBERED 0900 -> 0940 ON 2026-09-08. The user: "put the gagged one
  last, so it's the last thing the NPC see in our device."
  It is now the final device block of ours before 8000, which is the strongest
  position a hard speech constraint can hold.
  ⚠ The old 0900 number is why this file's notes below talk about "0900" -
  they describe the same decision, at the number it had then.
#}
{#
  VRTE DD/ZaZ AddOn - gag speech constraint.        (2026-08-23, fixed 23:30)

  DROP-IN, NOT AN EDIT. SkyrimNet's loader globs this folder, so this file is
  picked up without touching any SkyrimNet file. It ships from the AddOn's own
  mod folder at this same relative path, so MO2 merges it in and a SkyrimNet
  update cannot overwrite or delete it. Do NOT move it into SkyrimNet's folder:
  that directory is rewritten at runtime (see the .backup.<timestamp> files it
  leaves beside 0700_extra_instructions.prompt).

  Numbering: SkyrimNet ships 0150-8000 in this folder. 0940 places this AFTER
  every response-format rule (0500-0800) and before 8000_recent_state_changes -
  late, because a hard behavioural constraint has to outrank the format rules
  it contradicts.

  ⚠⚠ THE ALWAYS-ON BUG, AND WHY THE GATE IS NOT `!= ""` (fixed 2026-08-23)
  The first version gated on `vrtedd_gag_name(npc.UUID) != ""`, and the block
  fired for every NPC in the game. The log said exactly why - the rendered
  prompt read:

      Carmella is wearing {}, strapped over her mouth.

  A Papyrus decorator that returns an EMPTY STRING does not arrive here as "".
  SkyrimNet runs them through ExecuteAllPapyrusDecoratorsAsync into a per-entity
  cache, and an empty result comes back as an empty JSON OBJECT - `{}`. And
  `{} != ""` is TRUE, so the guard passed every time.

  So the gate is now the NATIVE `worn_has_keyword`, which returns a real boolean
  and cannot be `{}`. The Papyrus decorator is kept only for the device's NAME,
  and it is `isString`-guarded so a `{}` degrades to the noun "a gag" instead of
  printing braces into the prompt.

  ★ The rule worth keeping: NEVER test a Papyrus decorator's result with
    `!= ""`. Test `isString(x) and x != ""`, or gate on something native.

  Why the name still needs Papyrus: DD splits every device into a RENDERED half
  (what she wears - carries the keywords, has NO name) and an INVENTORY half
  (carries the name). SkyrimNet's own get_worn_equipment reports the worn record,
  whose FULL name is empty for all 770 DD devices, so it can say "something is in
  the mouth slot" but never what. GetWornDevice resolves the named half.

  ⚠ render_mode guard: a gag stops SPEECH, not THOUGHT. Without this the
  constraint would also muzzle her internal monologue, which is exactly when
  she is most interesting - unable to answer, thinking plenty.
#}
{% if render_mode != "thoughts" and exists("npc") and existsIn(npc, "UUID") %}
{# ★ 1.3.0 (2026-09-14): STATE FILE FIRST, decorator as the fallback. VRTE_DDZaZ.dll writes
   Data/SKSE/Plugins/VRTE_DDZaZ/prompt_state.json the instant a device goes on or off, a name
   arrives, a restraint is released; read_json re-reads on the file's mtime and the random second
   argument defeats SkyrimNet's 55 s callback cache (VRTouchEvents' recipe, VR-verified, report 45).
   Matched on the SkyrimNet entity UUID. No entry for her = the old decorator path, unchanged. #}
{% set _ds = read_json("VRTE_DDZaZ/prompt_state", random * 10000 + random * 100 + random) %}
{% set _de = 0 %}
{% if isObject(_ds) and existsIn(_ds, "npcs") %}{% for _e in _ds.npcs %}{% if _e.uuid == npc.UUID %}{% set _de = _e %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}{% endif %}
{% if isObject(_de) and existsIn(_de, "gag") %}{% set _vd_gagraw = _de.gag %}{% else %}{% set _vd_gagraw = vrtedd_gag_name(npc.UUID) %}{% endif %}
{% set _vd_gagok = (isString(_vd_gagraw) and _vd_gagraw != "") %}
{% set _vd_gagname = "a gag" %}
{% if _vd_gagok %}{% set _vd_gagname = _vd_gagraw %}{% endif %}
{% if worn_has_keyword(npc.UUID, "zad_DeviousGag") or _vd_gagok %}
{% set _p = "he" %}{% set _pp = "his" %}{% set _po = "him" %}
{% if decnpc(npc.UUID).isFemale %}{% set _p = "she" %}{% set _pp = "her" %}{% set _po = "her" %}{% endif %}
{#
  ⛔ TWO BRANCHES SINCE 2026-08-28, and the single branch before it was a live
  falsehood on 23 devices. The user, on #170 "Black Waxed Ring Gag": "did you
  made a new state for ring gag? Like speech is still possible? ... it's not
  really speech if your mouth is open, it's more like ... slurred, garbled, or
  open-mouthed / drooling speech".

  ★ DD MARKS THIS ITSELF and the census is exact: `zad_PermitOral` is carried by
  23 gags - ALL 14 GagRing, the 8 "Lips Gag" GagLarge records, and 1 Gag - and
  by ZERO bit gags and ZERO panel gags. The AddOn's own BlockedOral has honoured
  it since it was written, so the DLL's access line and this prompt were saying
  opposite things about the same mouth.

  ⚠ GATED ON THE NATIVE, not on a Papyrus decorator - `worn_has_keyword` returns
  a real boolean. See the always-on bug above: a decorator's empty result is
  `{}`, and `{} != ""` is TRUE.
#}
{% if worn_has_keyword(npc.UUID, "zad_PermitOral") %}
**MOUTH HELD OPEN - SPEECH IS BADLY DEGRADED, NOT BLOCKED.** {{ decnpc(npc.UUID).name }} is wearing {{ _vd_gagname }}, which holds {{ _pp }} mouth open around a rigid opening. {{ _p | capitalize }} CAN make sound and be understood with effort. The ring holds {{ _pp }} lips apart and {{ _pp }} teeth apart, so every word arrives shaped by an open mouth.

Write {{ _pp }} dialogue as genuinely slurred and garbled. Every sound that needs the lips or teeth is gone: b, p, m, f and v collapse or vanish, and consonants generally smear into the vowels around them. Vowels carry, so {{ _p }} is loudest and clearest on open sounds. Names come out mangled. Long or precise words fail where short blunt ones land.

{{ _pp | capitalize }} jaw is held apart, so {{ _p }} drools and {{ _pp }} speech breaks around it. Anything complicated may need repeating, or may be easier to convey by look and gesture than by trying again.

⚠ Deform the words ON THE PAGE so a reader hears the slur - that is the whole instruction. {{ _p | capitalize }} CAN be understood with effort, and writing that effort is the point of this state.
{% else %}
**GAGGED - {{ _pp | upper }} MOUTH IS SEALED.** {{ decnpc(npc.UUID).name }} is wearing {{ _vd_gagname }}, strapped over {{ _pp }} mouth. It holds {{ _pp }} mouth shut around it, so every sound {{ _p }} makes leaves as raw voice only.

EVERY line {{ _p }} gives is pure vocalisation: ("Mmmph!", "Nnngh-!", a long hum through the nose), and breathing. Tone, volume and urgency carry {{ _pp }} whole meaning — that is the entire channel {{ _p }} has, and someone paying attention can read it.

{{ _p | capitalize }} understands everything said to {{ _po }} perfectly and is entirely lucid. The gag takes the articulation and leaves the mind whole, so write a sharp, present person answering with the only sound {{ _p }} has.

It stays exactly as it was put on. It comes off only when someone else opens it with the proper key, and it holds just as firmly after hours as it did in the first minute — time is on the device's side.
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
